source: crates/standalone/fixture/src/lib.rs
---
Claim, prove, list and remove custom domains.

Usage: ink domain <COMMAND>

Examples
  # Ask to prove a name
  ink domain add www.example.org

  # Serve the site at it once the record is published
  ink domain prove www.example.org

Commands
  add     Ask to prove a custom domain
  list    The site's custom domains
  prove   Check the record and serve the site at the name
  remove  Stop serving a name, or drop its claim

Exit codes
  0  Done
  2  Wrong usage: no site named, an id that is none, a
     deploy the site lacks
  3  Not signed in, or the token was refused
  4  The API could not be reached or failed; safe to retry
  5  The API refused the change as it stands: the deploy is
     already live, say

Environment
  INK_API       The address of the API, as --api
  INK_SITE      The site's id, as --site
  INK_KEY       The private key to sign requests with, for a
                CI job; never a flag, so it stays out of
                process lists. `ink login` keeps one in the
                config folder instead
  INK_KEY_FILE  A file that holds that key, in place of
                INK_KEY

See also  ink status, ink repo
Docs      https://github.com/uses-ink/uses.ink/blob/main/docs/cli.md
Global    -C, --json, -q, -v, --color, --no-progress, --log,
          --log-file (see `ink --help`)
